MINIMUM IMPLEMENTATION (DoD 2). In packages/core/src/policy/approval-validation.ts add ONE exported function, roughly:

```ts
export function validateApprovalDependencyChanges(
  value: unknown,
): ApprovalDependencyChanges | undefined {
  const snapshot = snapshotData(value);
  if (!snapshot.ok) return undefined;
  if (!validDependencyChanges(snapshot.value)) return undefined;
  return deepFreeze(snapshot.value) as unknown as ApprovalDependencyChanges;
}
```

BINDING CONSTRAINTS:
- REUSE `validDependencyChanges` (:45) unchanged. Do not inline, copy or widen it, and do not export it — taskRail 1 forbids exposing the private boolean guard, and it is unsafe to publish because it reads an unsnapshotted caller object.
- Import `deepFreeze` from ./policy-validation.js (already exported at :95); `snapshotData` is already imported at :19.
- Import `ApprovalDependencyChanges` as a TYPE from ./approval-contract.js (it is already published at the root, so no new type export is needed).
- Snapshot BEFORE the shape check, never after: the order is what makes the getter/proxy arm refuse.
- Freeze the SNAPSHOT, never the caller's object.
- LEAVE `validateApprovalRecord` (:72-91) BYTE-UNCHANGED, including its unfrozen return at :90. DoD 2 pins it as the unchanged full 18-key admission and three in-package call sites depend on the current behaviour.
- Do NOT touch packages/core/src/policy/approval-validation.js — it is `export * from "./approval-validation.ts";` (42 bytes) and a star export already carries the new name. DoD 3 requires it byte-identical.
- File is 111 lines now; the addition keeps it far under the 250 target.
